<title>POLAND: Poland sells 8.4 percent of Tonsil shares.</title>
<headline>Poland sells 8.4 percent of Tonsil shares.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish bank Powszechny Bank Gospodarczy in Lodz SA bought 175,000 shares or 8.39 percent of the equity in speaker-systems maker Tonsil SA from the government, paying 15 zlotys per share, the treasury ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>The ministry still has 383,315 shares in the firm and other main shareholders are Japan's Tohoku Pioneer Electronic Corporation which has 13.34 percent of shares, and state-owned bank PKO BP which controls 9.08 percent. Bank Slaski has 6.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
